Yes, you can tell if a Slack message has been read or not using the Slack API endpoints. When you retrieve a message by its ID, Slack provides a `read` property in the message object that indicates whether the message has been read or not.

Here's an example of how to retrieve a message and check if it has been read using the Slack API:
```javascript
const axios = require('axios');

async function getMessage(messageId) {
  try {
    const response = await axios.get(`https://slack.com/api/messages.read`, {
      params: {
        token: 'YOUR_SLACK_API_TOKEN',
        channel: '#channel-id',
        message_ts: messageId,
      },
    });

    const message = response.data;
    console.log(message);

    if (message.read) {
      console.log('The message has been read.');
    } else {
      console.log('The message has not been read.');
    }
  } catch (error) {
    console.error(error);
  }
}

getMessage('message-id');
```
Replace `YOUR_SLACK_API_TOKEN` with your Slack API token and `#channel-id` with the channel where the message was sent.

Note that the `read` property is only available for messages that have been read by users in the channel. If the message has not been read, the `read` property will be set to `false`.

